{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"agent_message","text":"The **sponsor bears the economic shortfall**: if the fund’s unitary fee doesn’t cover its operating costs, the sponsor is contractually responsible for the excess.\n\nBut that allocation **doesn’t necessarily release the fund from its own payment obligations**. If the fund is party to agreements with service providers, it may still owe them expenses if the sponsor fails to pay; the fund may then have a claim against the sponsor under the expense-assumption agreement. The exact result depends on the governing contracts and any guarantees or indemnities."}}
